# F-B fix evidence - the nixos-autoinstall unit cannot reach the app (unit PATH)
Date: 2026-10-06T18:33:03.899Z
Worktree: /home/mei/nixos-wt/thinkpad-zero-touch-install-wave3 (base tip a1c86ad)
Brief: .omo/ulw-execute/briefs/wave3-fix-unit-path.md

## Root cause
mkApp (modules/flake/apps.nix:9-21) builds the app wrapper as:
  #!/usr/bin/env bash
  PATH=<git+pathDeps>:$PATH
  exec <self>/apps/x86_64-linux/install "$@"
The systemd service nixos-autoinstall.service (modules/flake/iso-images.nix) had no
service-level `path`, so systemd default service PATH (coreutils/findutils/gnugrep/
gnused/systemd) carried no bash: the wrapper shebang could not exec and the app never
started. The app first actions are `nix eval` (apps/x86_64-linux/install:175, :256,
:310, enroll()), so nix was also missing from that PATH.

## BEFORE (existing evidence task-14-thinkpad-zero-touch-install.log:2467-2468)
  > Oct 06 14:21:30 antagony nixos-autoinstall-start[1066]: env: 'bash': No such file or directory
  > Oct 06 14:21:30 antagony systemd[1]: nixos-autoinstall.service: Main process exited, code=exited, status=127/n/a
and the then-current assertion failed:
  > !!! RequestedAssertionFailed: command `journalctl -u nixos-autoinstall.service --no-pager | grep -F 'install: '` failed (exit code 1)

## Fix
modules/flake/iso-images.nix - systemd.services.nixos-autoinstall gains:
  path = [ pkgs.bash pkgs.coreutils pkgs.nix ];
(sibling of serviceConfig; no unitConfig/serviceConfig field changed - the t11 eval wall
pins ConditionKernelCommandLine/Type/RemainAfterExit/StandardOutput verbatim.)

## AFTER (new run)
Run 2 (tightened test) EXIT=0. `timeout 3000 nix build .#checks.x86_64-linux.iso-autostart-vm --no-link`
rc=0. gatedBoot journal (nix log .#checks.x86_64-linux.iso-autostart-vm):
  Oct 06 14:45:45 antagony nixos-autoinstall-start[1194]: Running install for x86_64-linux
  Oct 06 14:45:45 antagony nixos-autoinstall-start[1194]: install: cannot evaluate the flake at /nix/store/qdrblfbxgac0hcsyyb2frk3qdl9215cs-source
(the wrapper banner proves bash resolved; the app diagnostic proves the app body ran.)
The old journal had 0 of these lines and 14x the old token (see BEFORE).

Tightened assertions (tests/iso-autostart-vm.nix, gatedBoot):
  grep -F 'Running install for x86_64-linux'   -> PASS (fail-before: 0 matches pre-fix)
  grep -F 'install: '                          -> PASS (fail-before: 0 matches pre-fix)
All durable assertions unchanged and green in the same run: plainBoot inactive/ConditionResult=no,
rescue target inactive, no /run/autoinstall-done, empty data disk untouched (both variants);
gatedBoot ConditionResult=yes, unit is-failed with Result=exit-code, rescue target reached.

WHY THE HOST-MATCH DEATH IS NOT OBSERVED HERE (finding, not fixed by F-B):
  - App dies at its first action, the declared_hosts `nix eval` (apps/x86_64-linux/install:256).
  - systemd accounting for the unit: 282ms CPU over 25.584s wall, 7.1K outgoing IP -> the eval
    BLOCKED on the network; the baked flake inputs cannot be resolved offline.
  - The same store-path eval succeeds on the host (rc=0), including with --offline and under
    unshare -rn, because the host store already holds the inputs.
  - The VM test runs inside the Nix build sandbox, which has no internet; the shipped unit
    declares `after network-online.target`, so on real hardware the app proceeds to
    verify_host_match (todo 14's literal expectation) and dies there.
  - Therefore the DMI/host-mismatch message is NOT asserted (it is unreachable in this sandbox).

No `|| true` added; boot.kernelParams and every gate field untouched. git diff --stat: only
modules/flake/iso-images.nix (+7) and tests/iso-autostart-vm.nix.

